class InsuranceController{
  static RxString insuranceIntrodutionList="If you’re looking to draft or understand insurance policy guidelines, here are some key elements typically included:\n\n1. Coverage Details\nTypes of Coverage: Specifies what types of risks or losses are covered (e.g., health, auto, home).\nCoverage Limits: Defines the maximum amount the insurer will pay for a covered loss.\nExclusions: Details what is not covered by the policy.\n2. Policyholder Responsibilities\nPremium Payments: Information on how and when premiums should be paid.\nClaims Procedure: Steps to follow when filing a claim, including time limits and required documentation.\nNotification Requirements: How to notify the insurer of changes that might affect coverage.\n3. Insurer Obligations\nClaims Handling: How the insurer will handle and process claims.\nCustomer Support: Available resources for policyholders, including contact information.\n4. Terms and Conditions\nPolicy Duration: Start and end dates of the policy, including renewal terms.\nCancellation Policy: Conditions under which the policy can be canceled by either party.\nAdjustments: Conditions under which the policy terms can be adjusted.\n5. Legal and Regulatory Information\nGoverning Law: Which jurisdiction’s laws govern the policy.\nDispute Resolution: Procedures for resolving disputes between the policyholder and insurer.\n6. Additional Benefits or Riders\nOptional Coverage: Additional coverage options available for purchase.\nDiscounts: Any discounts applicable to the policy.\n7. Definitions\nTerminology: Definitions of key terms used in the policy to ensure clarity.\nIf you need more specific guidance or have questions about a particular type of insurance policy, let me know!".obs;
